 "human_notes": {
  "order": [
   {
    "note": "Both guides open the same way and it is unusually explicit: craft ALL FIVE tools before touching any food. 'You're going to want to make yourself a cooking pot, an all-purpose food press, a frying pan, a knife and a mortar and pestle.' They are taught as one set, not a progression.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:cooking_pot",
     "croptopia:food_press",
     "croptopia:frying_pan",
     "croptopia:knife",
     "croptopia:mortar_and_pestle"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Then two staple ingredients that gate huge recipe families and are easy to miss: cinnamon (found growing on trees in the world) and salt (produced in a furnace, not farmed).",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:cinnamon",
     "croptopia:salt"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Only then crops. Seeds come from breaking wild plants found while exploring - there is no crafting route into the crop set.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:strawberry",
     "croptopia:grape",
     "croptopia:coffee_beans"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "ladder": [
   {
    "note": "This mod has no tier ladder at all - it is a BREADTH mod. The only real progression is tool-to-recipe-family: each tool unlocks a whole category rather than a better version of itself. Four of the five tools are just iron.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:knife",
     "croptopia:cooking_pot",
     "croptopia:frying_pan",
     "croptopia:mortar_and_pestle",
     "croptopia:food_press"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Ingredient chain, the closest thing to a ladder: a flourable crop becomes flour, flour plus a water bottle in the cooking pot becomes dough, and dough plus the frying pan becomes the baked goods.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:flour",
     "croptopia:dough",
     "croptopia:pecan_pie"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "The food press is the most expensive tool (hopper plus piston, so redstone-gated) and it alone unlocks every juice and, with the cooking pot, butter. Effectively the mod's tier-2.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:food_press",
     "croptopia:orange_juice",
     "croptopia:coffee",
     "croptopia:butter"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "gates": [
   {
    "note": "Recipe families map one-to-one onto tools: juice = food press + glass bottle + fruit; jam = cooking pot + sugar + fruit; pies = frying pan + dough. Without the matching tool the entire family is unreachable.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:food_press",
     "croptopia:cooking_pot",
     "croptopia:frying_pan",
     "croptopia:strawberry_jam",
     "croptopia:orange_juice"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "The tools are consumed as recipe INGREDIENTS in the shapeless recipes rather than being placed as blocks - they are returned, but they must be in the grid, which surprises players expecting a machine to place down.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:cooking_pot",
     "croptopia:food_press",
     "croptopia:butter"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Salt is smelted, not grown - a guide stumbles over this on camera ('it says a blasting furnace? okay, any kind of furnace'). It gates a large share of the savoury recipes.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:salt"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Every crop is world-gated: seeds only come from breaking wild plants in the right biome. Fully grown crops can be right-click harvested without breaking them.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:coffee_beans",
     "croptopia:cinnamon"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "payoff": [
   {
    "note": "The click moment is finishing the five-tool set - the recipe book goes from a handful of items to hundreds at once. Guides describe 'three double chests worth' of plantable foods.",
    "ids": [
     "croptopia:cooking_pot",
     "croptopia:food_press",
     "croptopia:frying_pan",
     "croptopia:knife",
     "croptopia:mortar_and_pestle"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Drinks are the most-discussed family and the one guides visibly enjoy - juices, smoothies and especially coffee.",
